      <div type="clause" n="88.6a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 88.6a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 88.6a" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="603" ed="#liebermann"/>Legis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.c"/> enim est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.8"/>: qui inscienter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.9"/> peccat, scienter emendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.10"/>.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="95"><ref target="clause:Hn_90-11a">Hn 90.11a</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 603 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">603</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 70, 12<hi rend="italic">b und mit Engl. Original dazu</hi> 90, 11<hi rend="italic">a</hi>; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Gif þu agultest wið þine efennexta unðonkes, bet hit þin þonkes (Old Engl. homil. 12. cent., <hi rend="italic">ed. Morris</hi> 17); wer unwillig gethan, muss willig zahlen (<hi rend="italic">Heusler</hi> Instit. Dt. Privatrechts II 263)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 70, 12<hi rend="italic">b</hi> and, with the English original, 90, 11<hi rend="italic">a</hi>; cf. Gif þu agultest wið þine efennexta unðonkes, bet hit þin þonkes (Old Engl. homil. 12. cent., ed. Morris 17); wer unwillig gethan, muss willig zahlen (Heusler Instit. Dt. Privatrechts II 263)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">603</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">placitum <hi rend="italic">ohne Hss. fügt ein Wi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wi inserts placitum without MS authority</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">603</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nesc. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nesc. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_88-6a.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">603</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dat <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dat Lond</seg></note>
